  "scienceFindings": [
    {
      "caseId": "q3-16-a",
      "judgment": "KEEP",
      "evidence": "Whole DE/EN demand and expected response distinguish standard-potential/thermodynamic ranking from actual kinetic rate. Given dense adhering aluminium film limits material/charge transport; given porous iron rust protects less in this model. Neutral-environment use is conditional, chloride can disrupt the film, and alloy composition/local cells bound general conclusions. Fresh local damage with rapid neutral-environment regrowth supports temporary increased attack and possible repassivation, not universal immunity or a change in standard potentials of unchanged redox pairs."
    },
    {
      "caseId": "q3-16-b",
      "judgment": "KEEP",
      "evidence": "Whole DE/EN alloy model supplies chromium-supported passivation in aerated neutral conditions and a plausible oxygen-poor chloride crevice exception. CostR3/S1 and equal load/mass let the learner give a conditional use judgment, not a unique commercial recommendation. Film disruption and insufficient repassivation explain local risk. A new unknown acidic process requires new film-stability/corrosion data; an alloy name or standard potential alone proves no suitability."
    },
    {
      "expectations": [
        "whole-duty-1",
        "whole-duty-2",
        "whole-duty-3",
        "whole-duty-4"
      ],
      "judgment": "KEEP",
      "evidence": "Both connected contexts cover tendency versus rate, dense film versus porous rust/local exception, environment-based use and alloy/chloride/data limits. They support the entire existing explain-and-derive-use competence as own acquisition in both GK and LK. No broad claim that all aluminium/alloys behave this way or all stainless steel is immune is made."
    },
    {
      "judgment": "KEEP",
      "evidence": "The prerequisite route supplies electron roles, observed redox ordering, relative standard potentials and their limits, oxygen/acid corrosion and contact local cells. Supplied observations and thought models remain paper tasks; no real laboratory execution is credited. c95 introduces passivation/material judgment in its own method context. Its explanation and conditional-use judgment address one linked material/environment competence."
    }
